{"id":"chatcmpl-a2e22994-0630-46f1-a1b7-fb6093d788c6","object":"chat.completion","created":1795248299,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"```json\n{\n  \"highlights\": \"This task demonstrates a multi-model cross-validation strategy for medical image interpretation, where conflicting outputs from independent vision-language models are resolved through a dedicated verification step. The key insight is that disagreement between models is a signal to escalate rather than arbitrarily pick one answer, and that laterality/localization questions benefit from explicit trajectory reasoning.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When two independent models disagree on a finding, invoke a verification step to adjudicate rather than defaulting to either model's output.\",\n    \"For laterality or localization questions, prompt models to describe trajectory and anatomical landmarks (not just presence) to make the side determination auditable.\",\n    \"Use a second model as a cross-check specifically when the first model's answer is negative or ambiguous, since false negatives are common in subtle findings.\",\n    \"Frame the verification request around the specific conflict (presence vs. absence, left vs. right) so the verifier targets the exact uncertainty.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical imaging QA\": \"Always pair a primary image-reading model with an independent cross-check model; treat disagreement as a trigger for explicit verification rather than a coin flip.\",\n    \"Binary choice with spatial component\": \"Require the model to justify location/trajectory, not just the label, so laterality errors are caught before finalizing.\",\n    \"Conflict resolution\": \"When models conflict, escalate to a verifier with a precise description of the discrepancy and the anatomical expectations for each candidate answer.\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm whether the two model outputs agree; if not, route to a verification step before answering.\",\n    \"Verify that the chosen answer is supported by described anatomical landmarks (e.g., expected vessel region) rather than presence alone.\"\n  ]\n}\n```"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":531,"total_tokens":899,"completion_tokens":368,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":531},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":368}}}